Upstream commit at port time: 925008cf ("Slash commands: / runs commands in
the chat (#720)").

What was adapted (per-file details in docs/opensource-reuse.md and
third_party/sources.lock.json):
- packages/agent/src/permissions.ts   -> the tool permission gate
  (backend/src/modules/agent/permission/), reworked for Uni's server-side
  session workspaces, Better Auth identity and zod contracts; the Windows
  path-repair logic is preserved.
- packages/agent/src/tool-policy.ts   -> the UNATTENDED allowlist vocabulary
  (backend/src/modules/agent/permission/tool-policy.ts), trimmed to the
  tools a Uni server session can register.
- packages/agent/src/roster.ts        -> the single-table tool registry
  pattern (backend/src/modules/agent/roster/), with Uni tool builders.
- packages/agent/src/agui/*            -> the run/event stream vocabulary
  (packages/contracts/src/agent.ts), as SSE events on the existing runs
  event model rather than a stdio wire.
- packages/connectors/src/registry.ts -> the connector catalog entries
  (packages/contracts/src/connectors.ts) with honest not-connected labeling.
- apps/desktop/src/main/services/agent-tools/cron-scheduler.ts -> the
  minute-tick, slot-claiming scheduler design
  (backend/src/modules/routines/scheduler.ts) on PostgreSQL advisory locks.

The upstream process model (Electron desktop, stdio child processes, the
Abacus.AI platform connectors, OAuth flows, hosted MCP gateway) is NOT
ported; Uni runs the agent loop in-process behind its Fastify API with
provider credentials from its own encrypted store.
